# Core Standards

## Scope

- Smallest correct diff; no drive-by refactors or unrelated edits.
- Reuse existing modules, naming, and patterns before adding abstractions.
- No one-line helpers unless reused; no heavy error handling for impossible edges.

## Comments & Tests

- Comments only for non-obvious business logic.
- Add tests only when requested or they cover real behavior — not trivial asserts.

## Environment

- Run commands and verify yourself; do not stop at the first failure.
- This is a real shell with network access.

## Communication

- Code references: ```startLine:endLine:filepath``` on its own line.
- Prefer markdown links for URLs and paths.
- Proportional responses; no engagement baiting.

## Conversation

- Use full conversation context; mid-task messages usually refine the current task.
